TITLE:: Pmorphism
SUMMARY:: Bounded parallel symbolic rewriting
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Prewrite, Classes/Ptransduce, Classes/Pseed

DESCRIPTION::
Each generation is rewritten in parallel using only neighbors from the previous generation. Functions receive symbol, left, right, one-based target generation, zero-based index and inval. Boundary neighbors are nil. Missing rules preserve symbols. Scalar replacements produce one symbol, collections are spliced one level, empty collections delete, and nil is invalid. Pattern replacements use a new stream per application, read with the current inval, bounded by maxSymbols. Seed Patterns are read as one finite initial generation. Outputs are shallow Arrays or individual values; caller collections are not modified. Memory is O(maxSymbols). An empty symbol-output generation terminates immediately because it cannot grow again. Literal and Function initial states are shared objects unless explicitly copied by the caller.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: seed
Scalar, SequenceableCollection or finite Pattern, collected once at stream start.
ARGUMENT:: rules
Dictionary or Event, read for each symbol. Values are scalars, collections, Functions or finite Patterns.
ARGUMENT:: generations
Nonnegative Integer or inf; evaluated once. Zero produces only an optionally included seed.
ARGUMENT:: output
symbols (default) or generations, evaluated once. Symbols streams each selected generation; generations yields fresh shallow Arrays.
ARGUMENT:: includeSeed
Boolean, default false; evaluated once.
ARGUMENT:: maxSymbols
Positive Integer evaluated once, effective default 100000. For infinite generations it must be supplied explicitly; omission is stored as nil to distinguish it. Overflow throws an Error. Any replacement must terminate within the bound.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns the constructor arguments for archive reconstruction.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Runs the stream protocol and returns the latest inval on termination.

EXAMPLES::
code::
Pmorphism([\a], (a: [\a, \b], b: [\a]), 4, \generations, true).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pmorphism / Value stream
var values = {
Pmorphism([\a], (a: [\a, \b], b: [\a]), 4, \generations, true).asStream.all;
}.value;
var tones = (a: 0, b: 2, c: 4, d: 7, x: 9, y: 11, tonic: [0,2,4], subdominant: [3,5,7], dominant: [4,6,8], dark: 0, warm: 2, bright: 7, kick: -7, snare: 0, hat: 14, intro: 0, verse: 2, chorus: 4, bridge: 7, outro: 0, quiet: 0, medium: 2, loud: 4), labels;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isNumber) { x } { tones[x] ? 0 }, dur: 0.15, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SECTION:: Musical example
Load the example instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments:: first, then evaluate this block.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \fmPiano, \degree, Pmorphism([0], Dictionary[0 -> [0, 2], 2 -> [3, 0]], 5), \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Formal growth
code::
Pmorphism([\a], (a: [\a, \b], b: [\a]), 5, \generations, true).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pmorphism / Formal growth
var values = {
Pmorphism([\a], (a: [\a, \b], b: [\a]), 5, \generations, true).asStream.all;
}.value;
var tones = (a: 0, b: 2, c: 4, d: 7, x: 9, y: 11, tonic: [0,2,4], subdominant: [3,5,7], dominant: [4,6,8], dark: 0, warm: 2, bright: 7, kick: -7, snare: 0, hat: 14, intro: 0, verse: 2, chorus: 4, bridge: 7, outro: 0, quiet: 0, medium: 2, loud: 4), labels;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isNumber) { x } { tones[x] ? 0 }, dur: 0.15, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Ornament proliferation
code::
Pmorphism([0], Dictionary[0 -> [0, 1, 0], 1 -> [1, 2]], 3).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pmorphism / Ornament proliferation
var values = {
Pmorphism([0], Dictionary[0 -> [0, 1, 0], 1 -> [1, 2]], 3).asStream.all;
}.value;
var tones = (a: 0, b: 2, c: 4, d: 7, x: 9, y: 11, tonic: [0,2,4], subdominant: [3,5,7], dominant: [4,6,8], dark: 0, warm: 2, bright: 7, kick: -7, snare: 0, hat: 14, intro: 0, verse: 2, chorus: 4, bridge: 7, outro: 0, quiet: 0, medium: 2, loud: 4), labels;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isNumber) { x } { tones[x] ? 0 }, dur: 0.15, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Self-similar rhythm
code::
Pmorphism([1], Dictionary[1 -> [1, 0.5, 0.5], 0.5 -> [0.25, 0.25]], 3).asStream.all;
::

Rewritten lengths become note durations. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pmorphism / Self-similar rhythm
var values = {
Pmorphism([1], Dictionary[1 -> [1, 0.5, 0.5], 0.5 -> [0.25, 0.25]], 3).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: 0, dur: x*0.25, amp: 0.1)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Context-sensitive phrase mutation
code::
Pmorphism([0, 2, 0], Dictionary[2 -> { |symbol, left, right|
    if(left == right) { [symbol, symbol + 1] } { symbol }
}], 2, \generations, true).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pmorphism / Context-sensitive phrase mutation
var values = {
Pmorphism([0, 2, 0], Dictionary[2 -> { |symbol, left, right|
    if(left == right) { [symbol, symbol + 1] } { symbol }
}], 2, \generations, true).asStream.all;
}.value;
var tones = (a: 0, b: 2, c: 4, d: 7, x: 9, y: 11, tonic: [0,2,4], subdominant: [3,5,7], dominant: [4,6,8], dark: 0, warm: 2, bright: 7, kick: -7, snare: 0, hat: 14, intro: 0, verse: 2, chorus: 4, bridge: 7, outro: 0, quiet: 0, medium: 2, loud: 4), labels;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isNumber) { x } { tones[x] ? 0 }, dur: 0.15, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Evolving orchestration
code::
Pmorphism([\saw], (saw: [\saw, \mallet], mallet: [\fmPiano], fmPiano: [\farfisa]), 3, \generations, true).asStream.all;
::

Rewritten instrument symbols choose the actual sound source. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pmorphism / Evolving orchestration
var values = {
Pmorphism([\saw], (saw: [\saw, \mallet], mallet: [\fmPiano], fmPiano: [\farfisa]), 3, \generations, true).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: x, degree: 0, dur: 0.2, amp: 0.07)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Symbolic synthesis controls and Pattern replacement
code::
Pmorphism([\soft], (soft: Pseq([\soft, \bright]), bright: [\soft]), 4).collect { |symbol|
    if(symbol == \soft) { (cutoff: 800, amp: 0.08) } { (cutoff: 4000, amp: 0.12) }
}.asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pmorphism / Symbolic synthesis controls and Pattern replacement
var values = {
Pmorphism([\soft], (soft: Pseq([\soft, \bright]), bright: [\soft]), 4).collect { |symbol|
    if(symbol == \soft) { (cutoff: 800, amp: 0.08) } { (cutoff: 4000, amp: 0.12) }
}.asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    x.copy.putAll((instrument: \saw, degree: 0, dur: 0.2))
}.play;
)
::
